  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Peaceful Coexistence and Resilience Activity in Northern Uganda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Targeted post conflict communities are living together in harmony &amp; enjoy good mental health.The activity targets 14,400 households and families in both Lango and Acholi regions. Each target household benefits from three core interventions: 1) peace building, 2) trauma healing and psychosocial support, 3) economic empowerment.Strengthen the role of traditional support structures in use of consensus-based dispute resolution and building their capacity to deal with drivers of all forms of violence and harmful practices. Provide Mental Health &amp; Psychosocial Support Services that improve the social functioning of conflict affected households through the provision of psychosocial care, and trauma support. Empower conflict affected households through socioeconomic initiatives that minimizes their risk of relapse. Strengthen the roles of the existing referral networks that enhances project sustainability.</narrative>
  </description>
